---
import Landing from '../layouts/Landing.astro';
import { TEAM_SERVER } from '../lib/downloads';
---

<Landing
  title="Privacy: what dispatch.foo collects"
  description="What the dispatch.foo website collects, and where to read the team server's own privacy policy."
  path="/privacy"
>
  <div class="page">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="page-head">
        <h1>Privacy</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          This page covers this website, dispatch.foo. The hosted team server has its own policy.
          Last updated 12 November 2026.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="prose">
        <h2>This website</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>dispatch.foo sets no cookies and runs no analytics or tracking scripts.</li>
          <li>
            Our host keeps standard server logs, such as IP address, browser and the page asked for,
            to run the site.
          </li>
          <li>
            The light or dark choice from the theme button is kept in your browser’s local storage
            and never sent to us.
          </li>
          <li>
            Download links go to GitHub, which hosts the app’s releases. GitHub sees those requests.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>The app</h2>
        <p>
          Dispatch runs on your machine and sends us nothing: no account, no analytics, no
          telemetry. It talks to services only when you use them, with your own accounts: your
          coding agent’s provider through the agent you run, GitHub for pull requests, and Linear if
          you connect a project to it.
        </p>

        <h2>The team server</h2>
        <p>
          If your team uses team.dispatch.foo, its <a href={`${TEAM_SERVER}/privacy`}
            >privacy policy</a
          > and <a href={`${TEAM_SERVER}/terms`}>terms</a> apply. The server stores your team’s work
          only as end-to-end encrypted data it cannot read.
        </p>

        <h2>Email</h2>
        <p>
          If you write to <a href="mailto:hello@dispatch.foo">hello@dispatch.foo</a>, we keep the
          conversation to reply to you, and use it for nothing else.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>If this policy changes, the date at the top will too.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Landing>
